#! ia 1.0

@law design-semantic-tokens-only
  meaning
    says "Parts and code-lowering recipes paint exclusively with semantic or component @design-token classes: raw hex colours, palette utilities, primitive tokens, square-bracket arbitrary values and !important flags are refused in @part token lists, recipe.classes and recipe.overrides. In adapt mode, size, spacing and layout adjustments are reported as component-library gaps rather than written into recipe.overrides, and define mode is refused whenever the target @part already declares part.code-export."
    answers "Which styling tokens and recipe overrides are admitted when lowering UI parts?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Use semantic or component tokens only, forbid raw colours, palette classes, primitive tokens, arbitrary bracket classes, !important flags, adapt size/spacing/layout overrides, and define recipes over parts with part.code-export."
  subject
    subject-word recipe
    subject-kind definition

@law design-active-patterns-and-recipes-sealed
  meaning
    says "A @pattern or @recipe with standing proposed may run only inside an isolated scratch copy marked proposed and never emits code for an application repository; promoting a @pattern or @recipe to standing active requires an @approval seal binding its record identity and digest, and any workspace composing @approval-rule records alongside @pattern and @recipe must carry a rule covering both words."
    answers "When may a @pattern or @recipe be marked active and used to emit application code?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Require a valid @approval seal for every active @pattern and active @recipe, keep proposed records confined to scratch runs, and require an @approval-rule covering pattern and recipe when approval rules are present."
  subject
    subject-word pattern
    subject-kind definition

@law design-single-claimant-no-order-tiebreak
  meaning
    says "Every design node has at most one structural claimant: innermost matching @part instance (by exact case-sensitive part.figma-names, else part.name), else most specific @pattern, else unrecognised, with slot contents planned independently. Two @part records claiming the same Figma component set, or two patterns of equal specificity matching a shared node, are ambiguous and held rather than resolved by listing order."
    answers "How is node ownership resolved across parts, slots and patterns, and how are ties handled?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Enforce unique Figma component-set claims across active and proposed @part records, plan slot contents independently, and hold equal-specificity ties as ambiguous rather than breaking ties by order."
  subject
    subject-word part
    subject-kind definition
